<figure class="research-lineage">
	<section class="lineage" aria-labelledby="research-lineage-heading">
		<h3 id="research-lineage-heading" class="visually-hidden">Research ideas that help interpret Atlas</h3>
		<div class="lane">
			<p class="lane-label">Shared sequence</p>
			<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.11039">Transfusion</a>
			<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.09748">DiT</a>
		</div>
		<div class="lane">
			<p class="lane-label">Frame prediction</p>
			<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.01380">Next-Frame Diffusion</a>
			<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.01392">Diffusion Forcing</a>
		</div>
		<div class="center">
			<p>Working hypothesis</p>
			<strong>One posed, multimodal sequence model</strong>
			<small>Generation + reconstruction + geometry</small>
		</div>
		<div class="lane">
			<p class="lane-label">Generative 3D / 4D</p>
			<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.02981">ReconFusion</a>
			<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.10314">CAT3D</a>
			<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.18613">CAT4D</a>
		</div>
		<div class="lane">
			<p class="lane-label">Geometry</p>
			<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.14132">DUSt3R</a>
			<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.17242">LVSM</a>
			<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.11651">VGGT</a>
		</div>
	</section>
	<figcaption>
		These research lenses make Atlas easier to reason about. They are not a claimed genealogy. Atlas' exact architecture and training recipe have not been published.
	</figcaption>
</figure>

